#34600
@DThe @MVe@Wile@Md @DGa@Wte@Mho@Duse@n~
This chamber forms part of the living threshold of Kokudar's private
citadel. Crimson-veined stone, warm walnut, and ruby-violet glass
replace the sterile halls that once occupied this wing. Brass
ward-lines are worked into the floor beside practical benches, message
niches, and guarded doors. The color is rich without becoming
ornamental excess, and the air feels inhabited: servants cross between
duties, sentries change posts, and distant voices carry from deeper
halls.
~
