citadel. Tall shelves, crimson-lacquered cases, catalogues, warded
doors, red sealing cords, and low violet lamps create an atmosphere of
immense accumulated memory rather than dusty neglect. Records of
campaigns, creatures, artifacts, spells, failed experiments, and old
citadels are kept so useful knowledge is never lost simply because its
original crisis has passed.
~
