#34699
The Crimson Throne Hall~
The deepest formal chamber of Kokudar's citadel opens beneath a high
vault of crimson-veined stone and pale silver ribs. A long wine-red
runner crosses the polished floor toward a raised dais where Kokudar's
throne stands beneath layered banners of the Veiled Citadel. Ruby and
violet glass cast slow bands of color across the hall without turning
it gaudy. Elyria's ceremonial seat stands at the right of the dais,
while places are kept for Vaelreth, Kaelen, and the inner council when
Kokudar summons them. The broad approach remains intentionally clear
so the Veiled Blades can form an honor guard or defensive line at a
moment's notice. This is not a shrine. It is the working seat of
authority for a citadel whose master prefers decisions to pageantry.
~
